---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Parenting" description="What the parenting experts actually say — summarized from their Instagram posts and reels, with scripts you can use and links to every source. Starting with sibling fighting.">
  <main class="bg-[#0c0b09] min-h-screen px-4 py-14 sm:py-20 text-[#ece5d3]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-[#c9a86a]">Parenting, distilled</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[#f7f0dc]">Parenting</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#c9c0ad] max-w-2xl">
        The best parenting advice now lives in 60-second reels — and disappears just as fast.
        This section watches the experts for you: Dr. Becky Kennedy at Good Inside, Big Little Feelings,
        Dr. Siggie, and others — summarized post by post, synthesized where they agree,
        flagged where they don't, with the exact scripts and a link to every source.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[#8a8474]">Summaries, not transcripts. Every claim below links to the original Instagram post or reel so you can watch it yourself.</p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6">
        <a href="/parenting/sibling-fighting" class="block rounded-2xl border border-[#c9a86a]/30 bg-white/5 p-7 sm:p-8 hover:border-[#c9a86a] hover:bg-white/[0.07] transition group">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#c9a86a]">Topic 01 · Sisters &amp; siblings</p>
              <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#f7f0dc] group-hover:underline decoration-[#c9a86a] underline-offset-4">How to get siblings to stop fighting</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[#c9c0ad]">
                The honest answer from every expert: you don't stop the fighting — you change what it teaches.
                Why it's never really about the toy, Dr. Becky's 15-second pause and "fair ≠ equal,"
                coach-don't-referee, the 3-step toddler version, word-for-word scripts for toy grabs,
                hitting, and "that's not fair!" — plus the red flags that mean it's more than rivalry.
              </p>
              <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">Dr. Becky Kennedy</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">Big Little Feelings</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">Dr. Siggie</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">12 Instagram sources</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl text-[#c9a86a] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a href="/parenting/tantrums" class="block rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-7 sm:p-8 hover:border-[#c9a86a] hover:bg-white/[0.07] transition group">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#c9a86a]">Topic 02 · Big feelings</p>
              <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#f7f0dc] group-hover:underline decoration-[#c9a86a] underline-offset-4">Tantrums &amp; meltdowns</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[#c9c0ad]">
                First, know which one you're in — a tantrum needs limits, a meltdown needs regulation.
                Dr. Becky's permission to say nothing at all, the before/during/after playbook,
                mantras to keep your own cool, the brain science (full feelings, no brake, few words),
                and the honest split between the co-regulation camp and the "ignore it like waiting for a bus" camp.
              </p>
              <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">Dr. Becky Kennedy</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">PedsDoctalk</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">Dr. Siggie</span>
                <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-3 py-0.5 text-xs text-[#c9c0ad]">12 Instagram sources</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl text-[#c9a86a] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-7 sm:p-8 opacity-80">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#8a8474]">Coming next</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold text-[#ece5d3]">More topics, same method</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-[#a99f88] text-[15px]">
            "I hate you" and rude talk · Hitting · Listening without power struggles ·
            Deeply feeling kids. Each page will summarize the experts' posts the same way — synthesis first, sources always linked.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-7">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#f7f0dc]">The experts in rotation</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#c9c0ad]">
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Dr. Becky Kennedy</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/drbeckyatgoodinside" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@drbeckyatgoodinside</a> · clinical psychologist, founder of Good Inside, author of <em>Good Inside</em></li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Big Little Feelings</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/biglittlefeelings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@biglittlefeelings</a> · child therapist + parent coach, toddler/preschooler focus</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Dr. Siggie Cohen</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/dr.siggie" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@dr.siggie</a> · child development specialist</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Devon Kuntzman</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/transformingtoddlerhood" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@transformingtoddlerhood</a> · toddler expert, ages 1–5</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Dr. Willough Jenkins</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/drwilloughjenkins" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@drwilloughjenkins</a> · board-certified child psychiatrist</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Dr. Mona · PedsDoctalk</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/pedsdoctalk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@pedsdoctalk</a> · pediatrician, child development &amp; meltdown mechanics</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[#ece5d3]">Dr. Deborah Tillman</strong> — <a class="text-[#c9a86a] hover:underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/drdeborahpurposedparenting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@drdeborahpurposedparenting</a> · parenting coach, consequence-forward counterpoint</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-[#8a8474]">This page is a personal summary project. It isn't medical or psychological advice, and it doesn't replace working with your own clinician — especially if anything in the "more than rivalry" section sounds familiar.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
